  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;be non-zero numbers. If&nbsp;the point of intersection of the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> lies in the fourth quadrant and is equidistant from the two axes then&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
